  {
    "pkheadingid": 1073,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 1089,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152969,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 1089,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:31:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1074,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 1090,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152970,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 1090,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:31:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1075,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1091,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152971,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 1091,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours occur in the ovary.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:31:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1076,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1092,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152972,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 1092,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Presentation is usually with symptoms related to an ovarian mass. Occasionally, tumours are associated with hormonal manifestations such as isosexual pseudoprecocity {196747; 17581418}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:31:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1077,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1093,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152973,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 1093,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are rare tumours and their actual incidence is unknown. Most tumours occur in girls aged &lt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;years although they can also occur in women {32850222}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:31:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1078,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1094,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152974,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 1094,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:31:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1079,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1095,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152975,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 1095,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:31:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1086,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1102,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152976,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 1102,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are typically large, unilateral, solid masses with a grey-pink or yellow to pale-brown cut surface.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:31:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1080,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1096,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152977,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 1096,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Microscopically, these tumours show a variable and haphazard admixture of germ cells and sex cord cells {27458149; 33002849}. The germ cells are found singly or in small clusters and are large, with pleomorphic nuclei and ample, often clear, and PAS-positive cytoplasm; they resemble dysgerminoma tumour cells. Sex cord cells may form cords or trabeculae, hollow or solid tubules (sometimes resembling sex cord tumour with annular tubules), or cysts, or they may grow diffusely. Immunohistochemically, the sex cord elements are typically positive for sex cord markers such as inhibin, calretinin, and SF1. The germ cells are typically immunoreactive for germ cell markers such as SALL4, PLAP, OCT4, and KIT (CD117) {16538443}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:31:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1081,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1097,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152978,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 1097,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:31:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1082,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1098,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152979,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 1098,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:31:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1085,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1101,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152980,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 1101,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> an ovarian tumour consisting of an irregular admixture of dysgerminoma-like germ cells and sex cord cells not exhibiting the distinctive appearance of a gonadoblastoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> positive staining of the germ cells with germ cell markers and the sex cord cells with sex cord markers.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:31:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1083,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1099,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152981,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 1099,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These neoplasms are staged using the FIGO and TNM staging systems.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:31:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1084,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1100,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152982,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 184,
        "headingId": 1100,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most, but not all, of the lesions are clinically benign. Occasionally (~10% of patients), a malignant germ cell tumour, most commonly dysgerminoma, develops, usually in postpubertal patients {17581418}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T10:31:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]